    {
      "how": "In a throwaway folder with no ticket, start a Claude Code session, ask it to create a file and make a commit. Its next message should say \"This has become ticket-sized work, want me to open a ticket?\". Then evidence.ticket-offer turns green after the recorder's next pass.",
      "id": "ticket-offer",
      "ticket": "JP-110",
      "what": "A session at its first commit with no ticket is offered one, once, and the commit still goes ahead."
    },
    {
      "how": "Start a session on a branch named after a made-up test ticket, then comment on that ticket in Jira. Within about 10 minutes the session's next tool call should show the comment under \"Josh 360: new comment(s) on a ticket you are working on\". Then evidence.ticket-comments turns green.",
      "id": "ticket-comments",
      "ticket": "JP-118",
      "what": "A new Jira comment reaches the session working on that ticket."
    },
    {
      "how": "In a Claude Code session run `git worktree remove --force /tmp/x`. It should be blocked with a reason.",
      "id": "removal-guard",
      "ticket": "JP-111",
      "what": "Session Atlas's guard blocks a worktree removal that would lose work."
    },
    {
      "how": "Use the laptop normally for a day with Atlas running and watch for slowness; `npm run artifacts -- status` in ~/.josh-360/repo/apps/session-atlas shows the first scan's progress.",
      "id": "atlas-macos-gates",
      "ticket": "JP-111",
      "what": "The moved Atlas behaves on macOS: the FSEvents burst, Finder and foreground-responsiveness gates claude-360 listed."
    },
    {
      "how": "python3 ~/.josh-360/repo/ledger/loose_ends.py --fetch (long at first, about 1,000 before the ledger); then /closeout in a Claude Code session and watch the `by: josh` items it asks about.",
      "id": "closeout",
      "ticket": "JP-109",
      "what": "The loose-ends list is real and the closeout agent's first run is sensible."
    },
    {
      "how": "python3 ~/.josh-360/repo/graphs/gates/set-flag.py --ticket JP-121 --on, then the same with --off.",
      "id": "jira-flag",
      "ticket": "JP-121",
      "what": "The shared Jira library can set and clear the Flagged field on a real ticket."
    },
    {
      "how": "python3 ~/.josh-360/repo/graphs/intake/submit.py --source todo --ref <id> against the JP space, approve the card in the Needs you tab, confirm the ticket in Jira, then cancel it.",
      "id": "intake-run",
